A comprehensive analysis of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay has been conducted within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, focusing on semileptonic processes $B^0 	o K^0_s \mu  ar{
u}$, $B^+ 	o K^+ \mu  ar{
u}$, $B^+ 	o \Lambda^+ c 	au  ar{
u}$ and $B^0 	o \Lambda^0 c 	au  ar{
u}$. The paper reveals that current experimental data for branching ratios and forward-backward asymmetries of $B^0 	o K^0_s \mu  ar{
u}$ and $B^0 	o \Lambda^0 c 	au  ar{
u}$ align well with theoretical predictions. Furthermore, the analysis provides estimates of polarization asymmetries in $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decays.
